{
  "case_id": "2002-02-337",
  "document_hash": "2f3ebe18494be1430404e70e6d478024fac6c5450dbc9c7ae3250a8ff66c7816",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Supreme Court",
      "case_id": "2002-02-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f3ebe18494be1430404e70e6d478024fac6c5450dbc9c7ae3250a8ff66c7816",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f3ebe18494b-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:07 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court record",
      "case_id": "2002-02-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f3ebe18494be1430404e70e6d478024fac6c5450dbc9c7ae3250a8ff66c7816",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f3ebe18494b-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "DONALD E. PINAUD, JR., ESQ., Jacksonville, Florida; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nANDREW S. HAMENT, ESQ., Melbourne, Florida; on behalf of the Respondent.\nLISA S. BLATT, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Donald E. Pinaud, Jr.",
      "case_id": "2002-02-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f3ebe18494be1430404e70e6d478024fac6c5450dbc9c7ae3250a8ff66c7816",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f3ebe18494b-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case is about the vitality and scope of the rule of construction from Shamrock Oil that says that the removal jurisdiction to Federal courts should be narrowly construed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Donald E. Pinaud, Jr.",
      "case_id": "2002-02-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f3ebe18494be1430404e70e6d478024fac6c5450dbc9c7ae3250a8ff66c7816",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f3ebe18494b-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PINAUD: Well, Mr. Chief Justice, obviously it's our position that maintain in this case does mean that it should remain in State court, and we think it's for a couple of reasons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2002-02-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f3ebe18494be1430404e70e6d478024fac6c5450dbc9c7ae3250a8ff66c7816",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f3ebe18494b-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: And I don't think something that is ambiguous expressly provides otherwise."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2002-02-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f3ebe18494be1430404e70e6d478024fac6c5450dbc9c7ae3250a8ff66c7816",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f3ebe18494b-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: you're representing says, I don't want you, I want another representative. Then you can no longer maintain it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Pinaud",
      "case_id": "2002-02-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f3ebe18494be1430404e70e6d478024fac6c5450dbc9c7ae3250a8ff66c7816",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f3ebe18494b-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PINAUD: Well, I -- that's -- I suppose that would probably be the -- be the case, but I -- I think that's -- I think that's more -- that's more akin to dismissal. I mean, if an employee brings a case in State court and brings a case in Federal court, I mean, they can always -- they wouldn't be maintaining it if they themselves choose to -- to abandon it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Pinaud",
      "case_id": "2002-02-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f3ebe18494be1430404e70e6d478024fac6c5450dbc9c7ae3250a8ff66c7816",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f3ebe18494b-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PINAUD: Yes, Justice Ginsburg, but that would be the employee's decision. That would be no different than saying an employee can maintain the case in State court when --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hament",
      "case_id": "2002-02-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f3ebe18494be1430404e70e6d478024fac6c5450dbc9c7ae3250a8ff66c7816",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f3ebe18494b-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Since 1875, a defendant in a civil action has had a right to remove a case arising under Federal law to a U.S. district court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hament",
      "case_id": "2002-02-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f3ebe18494be1430404e70e6d478024fac6c5450dbc9c7ae3250a8ff66c7816",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f3ebe18494b-0001-0008",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The court below correctly ruled that respondent had a right to remove this case for three reasons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hament",
      "case_id": "2002-02-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f3ebe18494be1430404e70e6d478024fac6c5450dbc9c7ae3250a8ff66c7816",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f3ebe18494b-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "as a Fair Labor Standards Act case, unless Congress has expressly prohibited removal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hament",
      "case_id": "2002-02-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f3ebe18494be1430404e70e6d478024fac6c5450dbc9c7ae3250a8ff66c7816",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f3ebe18494b-0001-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Number one, Justice Ginsburg, at this point the Department of Labor has changed their position, and I think that's because of the addition in 1948 of the very express standard that except as otherwise expressly provided by an act of Congress, this type of case would be removable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Blatt",
      "case_id": "2002-02-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f3ebe18494be1430404e70e6d478024fac6c5450dbc9c7ae3250a8ff66c7816",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f3ebe18494b-0001-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The language in the Fair Labor Standards Act providing that an action may be maintained in any Federal or State court of competent jurisdiction does not expressly foreclose removal. Rather, it grants an employee a cause of action over which State and Federal courts have concurrent jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Blatt",
      "case_id": "2002-02-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f3ebe18494be1430404e70e6d478024fac6c5450dbc9c7ae3250a8ff66c7816",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f3ebe18494b-0001-0007",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There was division and there still is division today, but we think that the 1948 revision makes amply clear that what's required is an express bar."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2002-02-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f3ebe18494be1430404e70e6d478024fac6c5450dbc9c7ae3250a8ff66c7816",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f3ebe18494b-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And for those reasons, we would urge that this Court affirm the judgment of the Eleventh Circuit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-02-337",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2f3ebe18494be1430404e70e6d478024fac6c5450dbc9c7ae3250a8ff66c7816",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f3ebe18494b-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Thank you, Ms. Blatt."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2002-02-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f3ebe18494be1430404e70e6d478024fac6c5450dbc9c7ae3250a8ff66c7816",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f3ebe18494b-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I -- I think also that these public policy concerns that -- that Justice Breyer was -- was discussing, these are really very important concerns that we don't think should be overlooked."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-02-337",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2f3ebe18494be1430404e70e6d478024fac6c5450dbc9c7ae3250a8ff66c7816",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f3ebe18494b-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: I didn't ask whether they intended to. I asked whether they did."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2002-02-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f3ebe18494be1430404e70e6d478024fac6c5450dbc9c7ae3250a8ff66c7816",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f3ebe18494b-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't know why Congress didn't get involved in it, but I would think it would be because they thought maintained was express enough, that maintain was good enough."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-02-337",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2f3ebe18494be1430404e70e6d478024fac6c5450dbc9c7ae3250a8ff66c7816",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f3ebe18494b-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Was there ever a proposal made in Congress to give workers who have FLSA claims the same express provision that is there for railroad workers?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-02-337",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f3ebe18494be1430404e70e6d478024fac6c5450dbc9c7ae3250a8ff66c7816",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f3ebe18494b-0002-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 10:54 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
